/* book Worked example: Q: (a) A police CW radar works at 10.525 GHz and a car approaches head-on at 100 km/h. Find λ and fd. (b) An FMCW radio altimeter sweeps Δf = 100 MHz in Tm = 1 ms. Find the beat frequency for ground 150 m below.
   1. λ = c/f0 = 3 × 10⁸ / 10.525 × 10⁹ = 0.02850 m.
   2. vr = 100/3.6 = 27.78 m/s, positive because the car closes.
   3. fd = 2vr/λ = 2 × 27.78 / 0.02850 = 1949 Hz.
   4. fb = 2RΔf/(cTm) = (2 × 150 × 10⁸) / (3 × 10⁸ × 10⁻³) = 3 × 10¹⁰ / 3 × 10⁵ = 1.0 × 10⁵ Hz.
   Answer: λ = 2.85 cm and fd = 1949 Hz (about 19.5 Hz per km/h); the altimeter beat is 100 kHz. */
