/* book Worked example: Q: An X-band MTI radar has λ = 3 cm and PRF = 1000 Hz. Find the first two blind speeds in m/s and km/h, and the canceller response for a target closing at 10 m/s.
   1. λ = 0.03 m; Tr = 1/1000 = 1 ms.
   2. vb1 = 1 × 0.03 × 1000 / 2 = 15 m/s = 54 km/h.
   3. vb2 = 2 × 0.03 × 1000 / 2 = 30 m/s = 108 km/h.
   4. At 10 m/s: fd = 2 × 10 / 0.03 = 666.7 Hz; |H| = 2|sin(π × 666.7 × 10⁻³)| = 2 sin(120°) = 1.732.
   Answer: Blind speeds 15 m/s (54 km/h) and 30 m/s (108 km/h); a 10 m/s target passes with gain 1.73, nearly the peak of 2. */
