/* book exam traps: Saying MTI measures speed. A canceller only removes fixed clutter; speed needs a Doppler filter bank. | Mixing up blind speed and blind Doppler frequency. The blind frequencies are n·PRF in Hz; the blind speeds are nλ·PRF/2 in m/s. | Putting λ in centimetres into vb = nλ·PRF/2. | Saying clutter always has zero Doppler. Rain and sea clutter move with the wind and waves. | Assuming a double canceller is always better. Its wider notch rejects more clutter but also more slow targets. */
